          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How Often Should I Clean My Automatic Dog Feeder?",
            "text": "<p>At least once a week ensure your dog's food remains fresh and safe to eat. However, the cleaning frequency may vary depending on the type of food you use and the number of dogs using the feeder. </p><p>Here's a general guideline:</p><ul><li>For Dry Food Feeders</li></ul><p>Clean the feeder's food tray, hopper, and any removable parts once a week to prevent bacteria, dust, and food residue from accumulating.</p><ul><li>For Wet Food Feeders</li></ul><p>Wet food can spoil quickly, so it's important to clean the feeder after every feeding or at least once a day to prevent bacteria growth and odors.</p><ul><li>Disinfection</li></ul><p>Every month, consider doing a deeper clean by disinfecting the feeder with dog-safe cleaning products to ensure it remains hygienic. Rinse thoroughly to remove any cleaning residue.</p><p>By keeping your automatic dog feeder clean, you help prevent mold, bacteria, or stale food buildup, ensuring your dog enjoys fresh, healthy meals.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_W4dhBK": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Will The Automatic Pet Feeder Still Feed My Pet During A Power Outage?",
            "text": "<p>Yes, you can still feed your pet during a power outage by using an automatic pet feeder with a battery backup or feeding them manually. Preparing in advance with fresh batteries or an alternative feeding plan can help ensure your pet stays on schedule and doesn’t miss any meals during an outage.</p>"
          }
        },
